oduce extracellular matrix proteins, maintain serosal homeostasis, and facilitate fluid transport.\")\n4537: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000077 \"mesothelial cell\")\n4538: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000077 obo:CL_0000076)\n4539: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000077 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001136))\n4540: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000077 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000222))\n4541: \n4542: # Class: obo:CL_0000078 (peridermal cell)\n4543: \n4544: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000078 \"peridermal cell\")\n\n(Showing lines 4525-4544 of 35602. Use offset=4545 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Class: obo:CL_0000076 (squamous epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000076 \"CALOHA:TS-1249\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000076 \"squamous epithelial cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000076 obo:CL_0000066)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000077 (mesothelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000077 \"A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000077 \"FMA:66773\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000077 \"mesotheliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000077 \"Mesothelial cells, which morphologically resemble squamous epithelial cells, express both epithelial markers (cytokeratins) and mesenchymal markers (vimentin), reflecting their mesodermal origin. They feature surface microvilli and apical-b